digraph decision {
  rankdir=TB;
  bgcolor="#0d0e12";
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, fillcolor="#181a20", color="#343846", fontcolor="#e2e8f0"];
  edge [color="#3b82f6", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, fontcolor="#93c5fd"];

  history [label="1. Prior-journal learning pass (python3 scripts/stats.py at 2026-11-01T10:10Z)\nSettled 12 terminal: 2 WIN, 5 LOSS, 3 EXPIRED with pct, 2 bare EXPIRED. Sum +4.23%, win rate 28.6%,\navg win +1.51%, avg loss -1.12%. ASTER subtotal +4.20%. n=12 mixed setups -> no directional\ninference is taken from the aggregates.\nComparable ASTER folders, checked against their own review.md / trade.toml / decision_tree.dot:\n- WIN+1.26%_2026-10-27T0919Z_ASTERUSDT (SHORT LIMIT 0.7150 / TP 0.7060 / SL 0.7200): faded measured\n  supply with the stop 0.0022 ABOVE the 0.71784 regime extreme; filled and hit TP. This is the one\n  shape that has worked on this symbol -> today the same shape is used and the same stop-buffer rule.\n- LOSS-1.01%_2026-10-23T1024Z_ASTERUSDT (LONG LIMIT 0.6950 / TP 0.7060 / SL 0.6880): the stop sat\n  1.75 ATR inside the rotational band, was swept, price then ran above the TP.\n- EXPIRED+3.95%_2026-10-18T1535Z_ASTERUSDT (LONG 0.691 / TP 0.721): TP at a range EXTREME was never\n  filled while price peaked 0.7190 -> today TP 0.6986 sits INSIDE the 0.6972-0.6988 shelf, not at the 0.6972 low.\n- LOSS-1.50%_2026-10-23T1147Z_ZECUSDT and LOSS-1.30%_2026-10-19T1533Z_XRPUSDT: stops inside the\n  structure being tested, filled and stopped in the same or next candle -> stop placement was the\n  first filter applied to every candidate today, before EV.\n- EXPIRED_2026-10-18T1730Z_AVAXUSDT, EXPIRED_2026-10-28T0840Z_ZECUSDT, EXPIRED_2026-10-30T0845Z_BNBUSDT\n  (limits never touched): fill probability is carried separately and EV/order = p_fill x EV/fill.\n- LOSS-0.72%_2026-10-29T1149Z_BTCUSDT (ask-wall fade that lost when the wall was consumed): that is why\n  the SL-first branch and the neither branch are priced rather than assumed away.\nNot used as evidence: PENDING_2026-10-25T1228Z_CAKEUSDT and PENDING_2026-10-31T0901Z_XMRUSDT are\nunsettled (XMR expires 05:00Z today and is settled later in this run, after this decision).\n"
    fillcolor="#1e293b" color="#3b82f6"];

  extract [label="2. Chart extraction (image 261101_11h06m47s_screenshot.png, ASTERUSDT 1h, Aster feed)\nOwn pixel read, 1920x1080 RGB. Theme colours: bg 19/19/20, grid 30/29/31, red candle 173/69/70,\ngreen candle 30/124/87. Candle bodies isolated as 5-px runs, bars snapped to an hourly grid\n(6.5292 px/hour, 248 bars). Price calibration by least squares over 21 axis anchors -> residual\n0.00005; slope -9.2106e-05/px, intercept 0.744706. Time axis: day gridlines at 23:00Z (chart runs\non UTC+1, footer clock 11:06:46 UTC+1 = 10:06:46Z).\nValidation: (a) chart header O0.7019 H0.7023 L0.7015 C0.7016 reproduced exactly by the last bar;\n(b) TradingView's own visible-range extremes 0.7321 / 0.6587 reproduced as 0.7321 / 0.6589;\n(c) every sampled hourly bar matches Binance klines within +0.0010-0.0012, the consistent Aster\npremium; (d) the 10-29 20:00Z bar carries the crash that public sources date 20:24Z.\nExtraction limits: wick tips good to about +/-0.0004; two stray 2-px noise pixels were filtered.\nMEASURED STRUCTURE: 10d range 0.6587 (10-30 00:00Z) - 0.7321 (10-29 15:00Z spike, given back in 5h).\nSequence: chop 0.6900-0.7177 (22-25 Oct) -> higher highs 0.7187 (28 Oct 10:00Z) -> vertical rally to\n0.7321 -> crash to 0.6589 -> +7.8% recovery to 0.7100 (31 Oct 17:00Z) -> 17h box 0.6972-0.7057.\nLast 12h range 1.04%, last 6h 1.00%. Tags/24h: 0.6972 x3, 0.6984 x9, 0.7000 x10, 0.7016 x10,\n0.7045 x7, 0.7057 x5, 0.7071 x3, 0.7100 x1. Extremes: 48h high 0.7100, 24h low 0.6924, 36h low 0.6832.\nATR14h 0.00316 (0.45%), ATR48h 0.00449 (0.64%), median hourly range 0.00510. Box ceiling = 61.8%\nretrace of the crash (0.7041). Price sits inside the 27-28 Oct pre-crash congestion 0.6970-0.7150.\nLast print 0.7016-0.7018 at 10:06Z."
    fillcolor="#0f2a43" color="#38bdf8"];

  scen [label="3. Scenarios and level probabilities - jev_noul, all on the 2026-11-01T10:15Z state\n(exact propositions, 36h window ending 2026-11-02T22:00Z; separate overlapping yes/no, never summed)\n- rotation 0.6972-0.7057 with no hourly close >0.7080 or <0.6960 = 0.55\n- hourly close >0.7100 = 0.27 | hourly close <0.6960 = 0.32\n- touch 0.7100 before touch 0.6972 = 0.39 (down-first 0.61)\n- touch in 36h: 0.6986 0.77 | 0.7050 0.72 | 0.6972 0.69 | 0.7100 0.46 | 0.6940 0.33 | 0.6900 0.20 | 0.7150 0.19\n- 'the 0.6972-0.6988 shelf behaves as real demand (rebound 0.0040 within 6h rather than break below\n  0.6960)' = 0.59 | 'the 0.7045-0.7057 band behaves as real supply' = 0.54\n- 'higher-low sequence since 10-30 is an intact short-term uptrend favouring an upward resolution' = 0.59\n- 'the 0.7321 spike + crash marks distribution, so a break above 0.7100 is less likely than a break\n  below 0.6970' = 0.45 | 'price inside 0.6970-0.7060 at 2026-11-02T22:00Z' = 0.64\n- 'driven mainly by BTC/market-wide moves rather than ASTER-specific news' = 0.60\n- 'the box resolves into a 2% move within 36h' = 0.39 | 'continues compressing' = 0.53\nReading: a two-sided rotation with a mild downside-first tilt (0.61) and a slightly better-supplied\nceiling than supported floor; no scenario dominates, and the decision does not need one to.\n"
    fillcolor="#1e1b4b" color="#8b5cf6"];

  research [label="4. Research (agenda set by jev_decide, full dated log with links in research_log.txt)\nAgenda: positioning_structure 0.78 > aster_events 0.13 > no_research 0.05 > market_driver 0.03, conf 0.74.\nOne agent pass; every endpoint pulled 2026-11-01T10:12-10:13Z. Findings that moved the numbers:\n- hourly volume contraction 510k -> 110-160k ASTER under the 1.04% range.\n- Aster funding 0.0216%/4h = 4.3x the complex, 12 consecutive positive prints, +0.277% paid by longs\n  in 48h (Binance briefly negative in the crash aftermath). Longs are the crowded, paying side.\n- Binance OI -2.3%/24h, -4.6%/72h: deleveraging, no re-leveraging into the flat.\n- Depth to move 1%: Binance $623k up vs $1.03M down (bids 1.66x), OKX 1.76x, Aster symmetric.\n  Bid walls 0.6986 (Bn 180.5k), 0.6982 (OKX 186.6k), 0.6989 (Aster 58k), Bybit 118k at 0.6968.\n  Ask walls 0.7040 (Aster 133.7k), 0.7051 (Bybit 116.5k), 0.7100 (Aster 210.9k) + 0.7102 (114.3k).\n- Positioning heavily long: Binance accounts 62.3% long (+30%/24h), top traders 82.1% long (flat 12h),\n  Bybit 76% buy. Taker buy/sell 1.016/24h but 0.663 in the 09:00Z hour (sellers into the decision).\n- No ASTER-specific catalyst inside 36h; next unlock ~4 weeks out; the 29-30 Oct crash was market-wide.\nPost-research Jev (jev_noul): 'rallies into 0.7045-0.7060 are sold rather than breaking 0.7100' 0.78 |\n'Aster ask walls cap rallies below 0.7100' 0.41 | 'heavier bids absorb a test of 0.6980' 0.56 |\n'0.6986 wall prevents an hourly close <0.6960 in 24h' 0.50 | 'volume contraction -> rotation rather than\nbreakout' 0.72 | 'deleveraging -> rotation rather than resolution' 0.79 | 'crowded longs raise the flush\nprobability' 0.55 | 'downside resolution more likely' 0.57 | 'rally to 0.7050-0.7060 then back below\n0.7010 within 6h' 0.54 | 'dip to 0.6975-0.6990 then back above 0.7010 within 6h' 0.59.\nNOT FOUND and not used: liquidation heatmap / clusters (all sources key-gated or empty), Aster OI\nhistory (404), Aster and OKX account ratios.\n"
    fillcolor="#14261c" color="#22c55e"];

  freshness [label="5. Freshness / re-anchor. Chart captured 10:06:46Z; live re-fetch 10:18:31Z.\nBinance last 0.7002 (Aster-equivalent ~0.7015) vs 0.7018 on the chart = -0.23% drift, 12 minutes.\njev_noul: 'the ticket remains valid at the live price without moving any level' = 0.86 (likely, auto) |\n'the 0.23% drift requires moving entry/TP/SL' = 0.13 (unlikely) | 'structure still intact' = 0.90.\nAt the live price: P(touch 0.7050 before 2026-11-02T22:00Z) = 0.64 (down from 0.72) and\nP(0.6986 before 0.7122 | fill) = 0.68. The re-anchored numbers are the ones used in the arithmetic.\n"
    fillcolor="#1f2937" color="#eab308"];

  candS [label="6. CAND S (selected): SHORT LIMIT 0.7050 / TP 0.6986 / SL 0.7122 / expire 2026-11-02T22:00Z\nEntry 0.7050 = inside the 0.7045-0.7057 band that capped 8 of the last 17 hourly bars, just above the\n  Aster 0.7040 ask wall (133.7k ASTER) and inside the 61.8% crash retrace (0.7041) where the recovery stalled.\nTP 0.6986 = inside the 0.6972-0.6988 shelf (9 tags) and on the Binance/OKX bid walls (0.6986 / 0.6982),\n  NOT at the 0.6972 extreme (EXPIRED+3.95% ASTER lesson).\nSL 0.7122 = 0.2% above the 0.7100 recovery high, above the 0.7102 Aster ask block, i.e. the 0.0022\n  overshoot buffer shape used by the journal's one winning ASTER fade (Jev: 0.57 at 0.7110 and higher at\n  0.7122 that the stop is beyond a MEASURED extreme rather than inside the band).\nG +0.908% | L -1.021% | RR 0.889 | p_BE 0.5294\np_fill 0.64 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.68 | P(SL first) 0.10 | P(neither) 0.22, expiry branch ~+0.0015\nEV/fill +0.562% | EV/order +0.360% | neither branch zeroed: EV/order +0.330% | pessimistic 0.55/0.25/0.20\nwith zero expiry payoff: EV/order +0.156%. Positive in every variant; no fees/funding/slippage in the model.\n"
    fillcolor="#272015" color="#eab308"];

  candL [label="7. CAND L (rejected, but close): LONG LIMIT 0.6986 / TP 0.7044 / SL 0.6936\np_fill 0.77 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.65 | G +0.830% L -0.716% p_BE 0.4630 | EV/order +0.413%.\nRejected on one specific, evidence-backed reason: jev_noul put 'the 0.6936 stop is beyond a measured\nstructural extreme rather than inside the rotation reach' at only 0.36, and the jev_decide requirement\ncheck marked that stop 'contradicted'. It is 0.0012 below the 0.6924 24h low while the 36h low is 0.6832\n- exactly the LOSS-1.01% ASTER and LOSS-1.50% ZEC failure mode. Widths tested: SL 0.6915 (beyond the\n0.6924 low) gives p_BE 0.5504 with p 0.66 -> EV/order +0.381%, but Jev's head-to-head still preferred\nthe short 0.81 vs 0.03 for the wide long, and Jev's 'shelf is real demand' was only 0.59 versus 0.78\nfor 'rallies into 0.7045-0.7060 are sold'.\n"
    fillcolor="#2a1818" color="#ef4444"];

  others [label="8. Other candidates tested and rejected (same expiry)\n- SHORT 0.7050 / TP 0.6986 / SL 0.7110: EV/order +0.349% but the jev_decide requirement check marked\nthe stop 'contradicted' (0.57 beyond-extreme at 0.7110, only 0.1% above the 0.7100 high).\n- SHORT 0.7045 / TP 0.6972 / SL 0.7122: EV/order +0.343%; needs a full 1.04% traverse and its\nP(TP before SL | fill) is 0.57 against p_BE 0.5133 - the thinnest margin of all candidates.\n- LONG 0.6975 / TP 0.7040 / SL 0.6925: p 0.65, p_BE 0.4348, but p_fill ~0.65 and the stop sits on the\nsession low (the exact 'stop on the level' mistake).\n- LONG 0.6986 / TP 0.7095 / SL 0.6936: p 0.55 with p_BE 0.3144 - attractive on paper, but it needs the\nbox to break upward, which the 0.27 hourly-close-above-0.7100 estimate does not support.\n- MARKET LONG at 0.7002 / TP 0.7044 / SL 0.6936: p_BE 0.6574 vs conditional ~0.60 -> EV/order +0.013%.\n- MARKET SHORT at 0.7002 / TP 0.6986 / SL 0.7110: p_BE 0.8306 vs ~0.50 -> EV/order -0.365%.\n  A mid-box MARKET entry cannot be made to work: the 1.0% box does not pay for a 1% stop.\n- NO_TRADE: kept as a real option (Jev gave it 0.12 in the final decision). Rejected only because the\nselected ticket is positive under every tested probability set, not because abstaining was unattractive.\n"
    fillcolor="#2a1818" color="#ef4444"];

  checks [label="9. Contradictions, robustness, validation\n- Conflict recorded and resolved by specificity: Jev's coarse head-to-head 'the short ceiling fade is a\n  better-supported expression than buying the floor' came back 0.33 (leaning long), while its narrower,\n  testable stop-quality judgments favoured the short (0.57 vs 0.36 beyond a measured extreme). The narrow\n  judgments were used because they map directly onto the journal's two documented stop-sweep losses; the\n  direction question itself is a coin flip (down-first 0.61) and is not what the ticket needs.\n- Coherence checks run: every conditional was compared with the unconditional touch probabilities\n  (P(TP|fill) 0.68 < P(touch TP) 0.77; P(SL|fill)+P(TP|fill)+P(neither) = 1.00). The one derived branch\n  that looked inconsistent (an SL-first residual of 0.08 for the tight long stop against 0.33\n  unconditional P(touch 0.6940)) was not used to make the case; the candidate was rejected on structure.\n- Order-sensitivity / re-wording: the short ticket was re-tested at the live price (0.86 valid, 0.13 needs\n  level moves) and its conditional was re-asked after re-anchoring (0.68 vs 0.66 before) - the answer is\n  stable and does not depend on the capture-time price.\n- Wide-stop trap: EV is not manufactured by widening. At 0.7122 the ticket needs p_TP > 0.5294 and Jev's\n  lowest tested value is 0.55.\n- Two-sided evidence kept: book depth favours the bid side, positioning and funding favour the offer side.\n  Because the ticket is a fade at a measured level it does not need that question resolved.\n- Model limits stated: this journal charges no fees, funding or slippage and fills TP/SL on touch, so the\n  worst case is exactly -1.021% and no more; with a realistic 0.05-0.10% round trip the edge would shrink\n  materially. No liquidation or heatmap level is used because none could be obtained.\n"
    fillcolor="#2d1b24" color="#f43f5e"];

  forecast [label="10. Independent forecast (chart_prediction.svg / graphpoints.csv rows 11-01T11:00Z..11-02T22:00Z)\nModal path, CONTESTED: drift down inside the box to 0.6974 by 16:00Z (down-first 0.61, the 09:00Z hour\nwas sell-heavy, lower highs since 31 Oct 17:00Z) -> rebound off the 0.6986 bid wall to 0.7050 by 22:00-23:00Z\n(the 8-tag ceiling) -> rejection -> back to 0.6986 by 06:00Z -> grind 0.6990-0.7025 through 02 Nov ->\n0.7018 at expiry. Stays inside 0.6972-0.7057 the whole way, which matches the measured rotation 0.55,\nP(inside 0.6970-0.7060 at expiry) 0.64 and P(no 2% resolution) 0.61.\nContested markers carried explicitly: an hourly close below 0.6972 (0.32) takes the ticket to a good\nexpiry gain without the TP; an hourly close above 0.7080/0.7100 (0.27) puts the stop in play; a market-wide\nBTC move can reprice the whole box in one hour. The path was drawn from the scenario probabilities, not\nfrom the order: it happens to cross the entry and the target because a rotation does that.\n"
    fillcolor="#2a2338" color="#c084fc"];

  terminal [label="FINAL: GO LIMIT (PENDING)\nASTERUSDT SHORT LIMIT 0.7050 | TP 0.6986 (+0.908%) | SL 0.7122 (-1.021%) | RR 0.89\nP(fill 35.8h) 0.64 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.68 | p_BE 0.5294 | EV/fill +0.562% | EV/order +0.360%\nPlace 2026-11-01T10:35Z | Expire 2026-11-02T22:00Z"
    shape=ellipse fillcolor="#1e293b" color="#eab308" fontcolor="#fef08a"];

  history -> extract; extract -> scen; scen -> research; research -> freshness;
  freshness -> candS; research -> candL; research -> others; candS -> checks; candL -> checks;
  others -> checks; checks -> forecast; forecast -> terminal;
}